          "type": "caption",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "Orbit speed comparison"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "caption",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "Bottom-left switch compares planetary orbital periods from a bird’s-eye view."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "caption",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "Planets move far faster than in reality so orbits read on screen (~35 s for Earth at 60 FPS, roughly 900,000× real speed). Inner planets outpace outer ones, but ratios are compressed (Mercury vs Earth, Neptune vs Earth). Speed also varies slightly with refresh rate because motion follows animation frames."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "caption",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "Retrospective note: I likely misread orbital periods during build, so the mapping was inaccurate. I believed the simulation at presentation; later review showed otherwise."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
